# apps/web SOLID TypeScript design

Source of truth: `.agents/skills/solid-typescript-design/SKILL.md`

## Must

- **SRP:** Routes own the URL map; layouts own chrome; pages own section UI; hooks own process state; utils own validate/normalize/hash; `types/` owns shared contracts.
- **OCP:** Add a section by adding a route + page module — do not grow string switches in `App`.
- **ISP:** Keep prop interfaces minimal; do not pass unused props through UI components.
- Prefer composition and focused modules over inheritance for UI and pure helpers.

## Must not

- Force class hierarchies or a DI container onto small pure utils.
- Mix CSV/file I/O orchestration into shared normalize/hash helpers.
- Embed page-specific business UI inside `MainLayout`.
